  "content": {
    "id": "p47-q16",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "Olivia the fruiterer sells two fruit packs.\n\nPack 1: 10 apples and 5 mangoes ($\\$12$).\n\nPack 2: 15 apples and 4 mangoes ($\\$14.15$)\n\nDetermine the cost of 1 apple and 5 mangoes.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$6.15$",
      "worked": "Let $a$ be the cost of one apple and $m$ the cost of one mango, in dollars.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}10a+5m &= 12 &&\\text{(1)}\\\\15a+4m &= 14.15 &&\\text{(2)}\\\\40a+20m &= 48 &&\\text{(1)}\\times4\\\\75a+20m &= 70.75 &&\\text{(2)}\\times5\\\\35a &= 22.75 &&\\text{subtract}\\\\a &= 0.65\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute $a=0.65$ into (1).\n\n$$\\begin{align*}10(0.65)+5m &= 12\\\\6.50+5m &= 12\\\\5m &= 5.50\\\\m &= 1.10\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe cost of 1 apple and 5 mangoes is\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a+5m &= 0.65+5(1.10)\\\\&=\\$6.15.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 100
  },
